  "question": {
    "text": "The number of distinct real roots of the equation $|x+1||x+3|-4|x+2|+5=0$, is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$|x+1||x+3|-4|x+2|+5=0$\ncase-1\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x \\leq-3 \\\\\n& (x+1)(x+3)+4(x+2)+5=0 \\\\\n& x^2+4 x+3+4 x+8+5=0 \\\\\n& x^2+8 x+16=0 \\\\\n& (x+4)^2=0 \\\\\n& x=-4\n\\end{aligned}$\ncase-2\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& -3 \\leq x \\leq-2 \\\\\n& -x^2-4 x-3+4 x+8+5=0 \\\\\n& -x^2+10=0 \\\\\n& x= \\pm \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}$\ncase-3\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& -2 \\leq x \\leq-1 \\\\\n& -x^2-4 x-3-4 x-8+5=0 \\\\\n& -x^2-8 x-6=0 \\\\\n& x^2+8 x+6=0 \\\\\n& x=\\frac{-8 \\pm 2 \\sqrt{10}}{2}=-4 \\pm \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}$\ncase-4\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x \\geq-1 \\\\\n& x^2+4 x+3-4 x-8+5=0 \\\\\n& x^2=0 \\\\\n& x=0\n\\end{aligned}$<br />No. of solution $=2$"
  }
}